---
import WebsiteLayout from "../layouts/WebsiteLayout.astro";
import { siteUrl } from "../lib/urls";
---

<WebsiteLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms and conditions governing access to and use of the ImRabo website."
  path="terms/"
>
  <div class="space-y-12">
    <section class="border-b border-border bg-muted/30">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 md:px-10 md:py-20 lg:px-12">
        <p class="mb-5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">
          LEGAL / TERMS
        </p>

        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-6xl">
          Terms of use<span class="text-primary">.</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          The terms and conditions intended to govern access to and use of the
          ImRabo website, documentation and related resources.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-7 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-border bg-card px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>
          DRAFT — LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6 md:p-8">
        <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
          This page is a drafting framework and is not a finalized legal
          agreement. The responsible legal entity, applicable jurisdiction,
          warranty disclaimers, liability provisions and dispute-resolution
          terms must be reviewed and completed before publication.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-10 px-6 md:px-10">
      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          1. Scope and acceptance
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Define the websites, documentation, resources and services covered by
          these terms. Explain when visitors are considered to have accepted the
          terms and identify any separate agreements that apply to specific
          products or services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          2. Website information
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Website content is provided for general informational purposes.
          Product status, package compatibility, feature availability and
          technical documentation may change. Visitors should consult the
          relevant product documentation and release information.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">3. Acceptable use</h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Visitors must not misuse the website, attempt unauthorized access,
          interfere with its operation, introduce malicious content or use the
          website in violation of applicable law.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          4. Intellectual property
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Identify the ownership and permitted use of website content, branding,
          graphics, documentation and other materials. Specify any permissions
          or restrictions that apply.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          5. Open-source software
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Software published in public repositories is governed by the license
          included with the relevant repository or package. These website terms
          do not replace or override those licenses.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Review the applicable repository license before using, modifying or
          distributing open-source software.
        </p>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/imrabo"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="mt-3 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold text-primary hover:underline"
        >
          Explore ImRabo repositories ↗
        </a>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          6. Third-party services and links
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          The website may reference third-party websites, packages, services or
          resources. Their content, availability, terms and privacy practices
          are controlled by their respective operators.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          7. Availability and changes
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Describe how website availability, documentation updates, product
          changes and discontinuation of resources are handled. Do not imply
          uninterrupted availability unless that commitment is intentionally
          offered and supported.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          8. Disclaimers and liability
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Insert legally reviewed warranty disclaimers, limitations of liability
          and any applicable exceptions. These provisions must reflect the
          actual services and applicable consumer protection requirements.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          9. Governing law and disputes
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Identify the applicable governing law, competent courts or
          dispute-resolution procedure after legal review.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          10. Changes to these terms
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Explain how changes will be published, when revised terms become
          effective and how visitors can identify the latest version.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          11. Contact information
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Provide the responsible legal entity or project operator and a
          monitored contact address for questions about these terms.
        </p>

        <a
          href={siteUrl("contact/")}
          class="mt-3 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold text-primary hover:underline"
        >
          Contact ImRabo →
        </a>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl border-t border-border px-6 pt-8 md:px-10">
      <p class="text-xs leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Publication checklist: identify the contracting entity, define the
        scope, review intellectual property and open-source licensing, complete
        disclaimers, liability provisions, governing law, dispute procedures and
        effective date. Obtain appropriate legal review before publication.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</WebsiteLayout>
